{"type":"data","nodes":[{"type":"data","data":[{"debug":1},true],"uses":{}},{"type":"data","data":[{"slug":1,"metadata":2,"images":118,"html":244,"xml":288},"ISic000208",{"file":1,"uri":1,"title":3,"status":4,"editions":6,"editionAuthor":20,"type":21,"support":25,"objectType":26,"material":30,"condition":44,"dimensions":45,"layoutDesc":56,"handNote":63,"date":85,"places":89,"geo":99,"country":94,"provenance":91,"provenanceFound":103,"provenanceGeo":111,"provenanceObserved":112,"provenanceLost":20,"graphics":118,"region":119,"settlement":96,"repository":120,"textLang":134,"bibliographyEdition":138,"bibliographyDiscussion":179,"citation":182,"tmNumber":8,"letterHeights":219,"publications":225,"zotero":229,"keywords":233},"I.Sicily inscription 000208",{"_":5},"edited",[7,10,13,15,18],{"_":8,"type":9},"285300","TM",{"_":11,"type":12},"127525","EDR",{"type":14},"EDH",{"_":16,"type":17},"10900657","EDCS",{"type":19},"PHI",null,{"_":22,"ana":23,"ref":24},"funerary","#function.funerary","https://ontology.inscriptiones.org/type_of_inscription/Funerary","Three fragments of small, yellow/white marble plaque. Bivona's photo and edition records the plaque as being in two pieces, with missing text to the right and bottom. Since then, the plaque has been broken into three pieces, with two fragments now missing (a sizeable part of the 'D' in line 1 is now missing, as is most of the 'S' and the interpunct in line 3). Green discolouration due to application of modern inventory numbers. Rear is flat, face is polished. Top edge tapers upwards towards centre.",{"_":27,"ana":28,"ref":29},"plaque","#object.plaque","http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/objtyp/lod/259",{"_":31,"ana":32,"type":33,"subtype":34,"resp":38,"ref":39,"note":40},"Medium-grained, homogeneous, white, smelly marble, likely Parian-1, Parian-2, Parian-4. Digital microscopy: homeoblastic to heteroblastic fabric (identification based on pXRF, digital microscopy)","#material.inorganic.stone.metamorphic_rock.marble.calcitic_marble.Parian-1 #material.inorganic.stone.metamorphic_rock.marble.calcitic_marble.Parian-2 #material.inorganic.stone.metamorphic_rock.marble.calcitic_marble.Parian-4","stone.marble",[35,36,37],"Parian-1","Parian-2","Parian-4","#Coccato","http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/material/lod/48.html",{"_":41,"ref":42}," Petrographic imagery at ",{"_":43,"target":43},"https://iiif.csad.ox.ac.uk/viewer/isicily/ISic000208","",[46,50,53],{"_":47,"unit":48,"dimension":49},"11","cm","height",{"_":51,"unit":48,"dimension":52},"13","width",{"_":54,"unit":48,"dimension":55},"0.8","depth",{"layout":57},{"p":58,"rs":59,"damage":44},"Three lines of fragmentary Latin text. Large + shaped interpunct in line 1 (Bivona classifies this as a hedera). Bivona's photo shows an interpunct in line 3, in comma shape.",{"_":60,"ana":61,"ref":62},"chiselled","#execution.chiselled","http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/writing/lod/1",{"lettering":64,"dimensions":65},"Extremely neat, well-formed and evenly spaced letters. Letters have serifs.",[66,72,78,82],{"type":67,"l":68,"from":69,"to":69,"h":70,"unit":71,"atLeast":70,"atMost":70},"letterHeight","Line 1","line1","24","mm",{"type":67,"l":73,"from":74,"to":74,"h":75,"unit":71,"atLeast":76,"atMost":77},"Line 2","line2","29-30","29","30",{"type":67,"l":79,"from":80,"to":80,"h":81,"unit":71},"Line 3","line3","At least 24",{"type":83,"l":84,"from":69,"to":74,"unit":71},"interlinear","Interlineation line 1 to 2",{"_":86,"notBefore":87,"notAfter":88},"Imperial",1,300,[90,95],{"_":91,"type":92,"ref":93,"region":94},"Thermae Himeraeae","ancient","http://pleiades.stoa.org/places/462513","Sicilia",{"_":96,"type":97,"ref":98,"region":94},"Termini Imerese","modern","http://sws.geonames.org/6539140",[100],[101,102],37.98365,13.69555,{"_":104,"type":105,"subtype":106,"when":107,"ref":108,"geo":20},"Found with  in Termini Imerese in the piano di Si. Antonio, during the works for the construction of new buildings.","found","discovered","1889",{"_":109,"target":110},"ISic000246","http://sicily.classics.ox.ac.uk/inscription/ISic000246",[],{"_":113,"type":114,"subtype":115,"when":116,"resp":117,"geo":20},"Antoniou, 2023-07-07. In the Depositi of Museo Civico Baldassare Romano, room 1, scaffold 13, shelf 3","observed","autopsied","2023-07-07","#AA",[],"Sicily",{"_":121,"role":122,"ref":123,"museum":124},"Museo Civico Baldassare Romano","museum","http://sicily.classics.ox.ac.uk/museum/066",{"slug":125,"type":122,"name":121,"uri":123,"description":126,"location":127},"066","A large and well-displayed collection. It begins with three ante-rooms, in the first of which is a rich display of lithics (mainly Neolithic) from the surrounding area. A display of material from Himera (lion-head spouts from the Temple of Victory and red-figure craters being the principle pieces) and a numismatic gallery then follow before the main room which contains Hellenistic and Roman material from Termini Imerese itself. Small finds, sculpture and inscriptions predominate. The museum collection continues upstairs with non-archaeological material (and a single inscription). The courtyard of the building holds a large collection of architectural pieces and inscriptions",{"settlement":96,"region":128,"country":129,"address":130,"geo":131},"Palermo","Italy","Via Marco Tullio Cicerone, 90018 - Termini Imerese (PA)",{"lat":132,"lon":133},37.98655109,13.69587845,{"_":135,"mainLang":136,"languages":137},"Latin","la",[135],{"type":139,"bibl":140},"edition",[141,155,167],{"type":142,"n":143,"date":144,"citedRange":145,"ptr":146,"ref":148,"inscriptionDate":150,"title":151,"author":44,"citation":152,"uri":153,"year":154},"bulletin","AE","1888-","781",{"target":147},"https://www.zotero.org/groups/382445/items/R46KDTZX",{"_":149,"target":149},"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001283","1994","L'année épigraphique: revue des publications épigraphiques relatives a l'antiquité romaine.","\u003Cspan>« L’année épigraphique: revue des publications épigraphiques relatives a l’antiq